WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.621
Lady Anne was a good rider and managed to keep her seat as Lizzie took off down the road.

2
00:00:07.622 --> 00:00:11.467
But I could see that it wouldn't be easy for her to regain control.

3
00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:14.775
And an out-of-control horse is very dangerous.

4
00:00:14.776 --> 00:00:20.827
I let out several loud, shrill neighs, pawing the ground anxiously.

5
00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:25.471
A few seconds later, Blantyre came racing back down the path.

6
00:00:25.472 --> 00:00:30.555
"Oh no!" he exclaimed as he saw Lizzie galloping off with Anne.

7
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:34.206
He flung the reins over my head and scrambled into the saddle.

8
00:00:34.207 --> 00:00:38.603
As soon as his feet were in the stirrups, I burst into a gallop.

9
00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:43.064
Blantyre gave me a free rein, seeing that I knew what to do.

10
00:00:43.065 --> 00:00:49.321
We raced after the runaways. For the first mile, we barely kept them in view.

11
00:00:49.322 --> 00:00:53.538
I was galloping as fast as I could, but Lizzie was even faster.

12
00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:58.680
Then the road curved to the right, and we lost sight of them.

13
00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:02.254
By the time we reached the curve, Lizzie had disappeared.

14
00:01:02.255 --> 00:01:06.623
The road split just ahead, and I wasn't sure which way to go.

15
00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:08.993
There was a woman standing at her garden gate.

16
00:01:08.994 --> 00:01:12.499
"To the right!" she called when she saw us.

17
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.719
"Thanks!" Blantyre called back.

18
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.252
We galloped on. For a while we barely caught sight of Lizzie.

19
00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:25.721
Luckily, after we'd lost them yet again, a road worker waved us down.

20
00:01:25.722 --> 00:01:33.841
"They turned that way, sir!" the worker called to Blantyre, pointing to an open area with lots of weeds and holes.

21
00:01:33.842 --> 00:01:36.881
It was the worst possible place for a gallop.

22
00:01:36.882 --> 00:01:41.434
When Lady Anne rode me there, we never went faster than a walk.

23
00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:44.570
We soon caught sight of Lizzie again.

24
00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:50.734
Lady Anne was still in the saddle, but she was swaying back and forth now, looking exhausted.

25
00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:55.234
I could see that she was pulling on the reins, but it wasn't doing any good.

26
00:01:55.235 --> 00:02:01.355
Lizzie was still going, though the roughness of the ground had forced her to slow from a gallop to a canter.

27
00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:06.446
That meant I had a chance to catch her. I surged forward.

28
00:02:06.447 --> 00:02:12.219
Blantyre had let me choose my own way while we were on the road, but now he took over again.

29
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:17.647
With a light hand and a quick eye, he guided me expertly over the tricky ground.

30
00:02:17.648 --> 00:02:22.558
I barely had to slow down. We started to gain on Lizzie.

31
00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:26.187
About halfway across the open area was a wide ditch.

32
00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:29.252
I thought it might make Lizzie stop at last.

33
00:02:29.253 --> 00:02:35.999
Instead she leaped awkwardly across, stumbling on the rough ground on the far side.

34
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.564
Lady Anne was flung to the ground and lay still.

35
00:02:39.565 --> 00:02:48.745
Blantyre groaned. "Now, Black Auster, do your best!" he urged me.

36
00:02:48.746 --> 00:02:52.872
I cleared the ditch with a strong leap, landing safely.

37
00:02:52.873 --> 00:02:56.306
Blantyre pulled me to a stop and leaped down.

38
00:02:56.307 --> 00:03:03.033
He ran to Lady Anne's side while I stood there, my sides heaving after the long gallop.

39
00:03:03.034 --> 00:03:06.336
Two men had been trimming weeds nearby.

40
00:03:06.337 --> 00:03:11.016
One was already chasing Lizzie, who had slowed down after losing her rider.

41
00:03:11.017 --> 00:03:13.511
The other ran toward us.

42
00:03:13.512 --> 00:03:18.464
"Oh no!" he said when he saw Lady Anne lying there still and pale.

43
00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:20.574
"How can I help?"

44
00:03:20.575 --> 00:03:23.689
"Can you ride?" Blantyre asked.

45
00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:28.841
"Not very well," the man said. "But I'll give it a try for Lady Anne's sake.

46
00:03:28.842 --> 00:03:32.118
She's always been so kind to my family."

47
00:03:32.119 --> 00:03:38.361
"Don't worry, this horse will take care of you," Blantyre said, gesturing to me.

48
00:03:38.362 --> 00:03:44.487
"Ride quickly to the doctor's house, then go to Earlshall and let them know what's happened."

49
00:03:44.488 --> 00:03:46.917
The man agreed and mounted.

50
00:03:46.918 --> 00:03:51.298
He wasn't a very good rider, but I didn't mind.

51
00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:57.165
We hurried to the doctor's house, and then back to Earlshall Park.

52
00:03:57.166 --> 00:04:06.153
A groom returned me to the stable while another quickly saddled Ginger for Lady Anne's brother and the others prepared the carriage.

53
00:04:06.154 --> 00:04:09.815
It seemed to take a long time before anyone returned.

54
00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:13.715
At last Ginger arrived back at the stable.

55
00:04:13.716 --> 00:04:17.364
"We galloped almost all the way there," she told me.

56
00:04:17.365 --> 00:04:20.557
"Lady Anne still wasn't moving.

57
00:04:20.558 --> 00:04:24.735
But the doctor was tending to her, and I heard him say she wasn't dead.

58
00:04:24.736 --> 00:04:29.879
Later I heard someone else say that she was lucky she hadn't broken any bones.

59
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.772
So I expect she'll be all right."

60
00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:37.050
The next day Blantyre came to see me.

61
00:04:37.051 --> 00:04:42.716
"You're the finest horse I know, Black Auster," he said as he patted me fondly.

62
00:04:42.717 --> 00:04:46.689
"You seemed to understand the danger as well as I did.

63
00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:51.009
Thanks to your speed and heart, Anne will be fine in a week or two.

64
00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:58.686
And from now on, I'm sure she won't ever want to ride any other horse but you."

